      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Printed sideways on both pages; read from rotated crops. Rows on p.50 end with Liuhokow; p.51 begins with Shantung. \"..\" = ditto as printed.",
        "Row Kailan, col 1920: last digit damaged (\"4,416,00?\", 9 or 3) — left blank.",
        "Row Liukiang, col 1924: last digit cut off (\"124,00?\") — left blank.",
        "Row Yentai, col 1925: first glyph broken but read as 1 (117,700).",
        "Row Yentai, col 1926: no figure printed. Rows Peking Syndicate and Chungyuan, col 1926: a single figure 116,773 is printed bracketed against both rows; put in the Peking Syndicate row, Chungyuan left blank.",
        "Row Pinghsiang, col 1925: last digit damaged (\"386,23?\") — left blank.",
        "Row Chiawang, col 1923: last digit damaged (\"183,46?\") — left blank.",
        "Totals: the \"Total of all actual production\" rows exceed the sums of the listed mines for Bituminous in every year (they evidently include mines not listed); Lignite total equals the Chalainor row in every year — reconciles.",
        "Lignite + Bituminous + Anthracite = printed Total in 1920, 1921, 1923, 1924, 1925 — reconciles. 1922: parts sum to 15,097,414 vs printed 15,097,420 — does NOT reconcile (diff 6). 1926: parts sum to 14,308,538 vs printed 14,481,521 — does NOT reconcile (diff 172,983, equal to the Peipiao 1926 figure).",
        "Total + Estimated native small mines = Total production of China in every year 1920-1926 — reconciles.",
        "1926 Anthracite: listed anthracite mines sum to 1,185,312 vs printed 1,185,292 (diff 20)."
      ],
